	(text "NOTES\n1. PS1: industry-standard SIP pinout assumed (1 GND, 2 VIN, 4 -VO, 5 0V, 6 +VO).\n   Verify against the A0515S-1WR3 datasheet drawing before layout.\n2. ISO_GND (isolated, 3-bar symbol) and GND (MCU side, triangle) must stay separate.\n   Only U2, PS1 and R9 cross the isolation barrier.\n3. U3 (AD5693R): I2C address 0x4C (A0 = ISO_GND). Set the GAIN bit (DB11) for 0-5 V.\n   LDAC tied low (immediate update), RESET tied high.\n4. U4 (TMP117): I2C address 0x48 (ADD0 = ISO_GND). Place right next to J1 on a shared\n   copper pour; leave its thermal pad unsoldered for best accuracy.\n5. Vamp = Vdac x (1 + R5/R6) - VREF x (R5/R6) = 1.2 x Vdac - 0.5 V (VREF = 2.5 V).\n   TC+ = Vamp x R8 / (R7 + R8) = Vamp / 101, approx. -4.95 mV to +54.5 mV.\n   Two-point calibrate in firmware; resistor tempco matters more than tolerance.\n6. R9/J4: bleed ISO_GND to the receiver/chassis ground only if the receiver input is\n   fully floating; otherwise leave J4 unconnected.\n7. Run N-type extension wire from J1 to the receiver.\n8. U1 SS pin open = internal soft start; U1 EP to ISO_GND.\n9. Footprints are KiCad library defaults: check U1 EP, U4 WSON, PS1 and J4."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 443.738 121.92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
